  - These guide what you write, but should never appear in the output`}}var TY,XP="**Before anything else, finish a partly written artifact**:\n   - An artifact whose output is a glob pattern (e.g. `specs/**/*.md`) reads `done` as soon as one matching file exists, so a run interrupted while writing its files leaves it `done` with some still missing\n   - For each such `done` artifact, first get its instructions and read any completed dependencies needed to determine the expected files. Then compare those files with `artifactPaths.<id>.existingOutputPaths`. For spec-driven's `specs`, read the proposal and check for one `specs/<capability-path>/spec.md` per capability it lists; resolve each expected path against `changeRoot` before comparing path identity, and verify each one remains inside `changeRoot` after resolving symlinks, both in its parent directories and in the file itself if it already exists\n   - Never write an expected path that fails that check; stop and tell the user. If any are missing, write only the missing files, each at its checked path - when the `instruction` field delegates creation to a skill or command, invoke it only if it can write each file to its checked path; otherwise stop and tell the user - and STOP - that counts as this invocation's ONE artifact. If you cannot tell whether a file was left out on purpose, ask the user";var QP=S(()=>{pn();TY=le("apply","You can now implement this change with `/opsx:apply`.",'You can now implement this change - `openspec instructions apply --change "<name>" --json` returns the tasks and how to work them.')+" "+le("archive","Once implementation and any tracked work are complete, archive it with `/opsx:archive`.",'Once implementation and any tracked work are complete, archive it with `openspec archive "<name>"`.')});function lb(){return`Implement tasks from an OpenSpec change.

